{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: exact D head 4820c13b068bbe7dc8fe68efee60aa1d77ec29ab on builder/typed-browser-models-t0d-20261109, all 14 artifacts, for DX-T0 item 3 of request 6f87a4e3 under promise 00b5bef0 and review request 0cc0ad39. Counter and Lending now read act names, field types, enums, limits and Lending's action lists from their authored definitions. Refusal wording moves into per-act annotation tables with unchanged words. The head follows ruling ac586d65.\n\nWhat I checked in the source:\n\n- Counter. `model.ts` takes `Control`, the failure reasons, the participant and board states, and every numeric bound from `countingCommitments`. `proposed` calls `shapeDeclaredAct` and `expectedOf` once per act and keeps the two missing-item refusals. Every refusal goes through `refuseProposal(kind, reason)`, and `annotations.ts` holds the same 23 sentences as main. The added `!own` test in `commit` changes nothing, because `canCommit` already requires an owned participant.\n- Lending. `NAME_BYTES`, `DESCRIPTION_BYTES`, `REASON_BYTES`, the staff grant and the library limit in the full-library sentence come from `lending`. `actsFor` keeps the non-genesis acts that read a thing and whose state guards on that thing admit its state. `propose` derives `expected` through `expectedOf` instead of hand-written revision maps. `refusalWords` is now `annotatedRefusal`, with an own-key lookup and the same fallback.\n- The compiler examples. `checkProposalTypes` in each model's test file rejects a genesis act, a wrong field type, and an unknown failure reason or act key. No test calls them.\n\nWhat holds:\n\n- Scope. Main a5b82ee0 is an ancestor, the head is pushed, and the builder's worktree is clean at the head. Against main, the head changes exactly the 14 paths that its 14 artifacts cover. The commit-message check passes: 7 checked, 0 flagged. No kernel, pin, retained JSON or client package file changes.\n- The values. I compared the `rows` arrays of `main19dd.stdout`, `headDcfa.stdout` and `headFinal.stdout`. All three hold the same 109 rows, including action-list order, every Lending proposal's `expected` map and content, and every refusal sentence. The baseline checkout 0b72dffc has tree a7af981d, which is main 19ddc868's tree. All four final-capture exits read 0.\n- The gate. I read gate.exit at 9b92bd28, tree c532751f: \"exit 0\". The driver and launcher exits read 0 too. The reconciliation records 5,838 passes and three expected skips, 45 compiler contexts, 16 typecheck scripts, zero reconciliation issues and both definition pins unchanged. The selector ran no Scale case. Only the note and three evidence manifests change between 9b92bd28 and the head.\n- The browser. GitHub reports Page run 42805991861 attempt 1 as successful, 12 of 12 steps, and Card run 42805991887 attempt 1 as successful, 13 of 13 steps, both on push at 1088dc06. Only the note and one evidence manifest change between 1088dc06 and 9b92bd28.\n- The evidence. The seven manifests verify. Their 32 recorded files match their sizes and digests and are read-only, and the credential scan finds no match. The first focus at 8292fe9a stays recorded as failed.\n\nArchitecture: sound. The authored definition is now the one source of each name and limit that the two browser models used to copy, and wording stays outside the pinned data. A later definition change moves the browser model with it, and the compiler examples catch a model that names an act or value the definition lacks.\n\nSecurity: no finding. The models still only propose. The native declaration judges every grant, guard and field, and the signing client shapes again before it signs. Annotation lookups use own keys.\n\nSimplification: no required change. Three notes:\n\n- Each `proposalAnnotations` table maps every act to one shared table, so the per-act layer adds no distinct wording yet. It costs little and gives DX-B1 a place for per-act reasons.\n- In Lending, `propose` now calls `shapeDeclaredAct` outside `act`'s try block, so a `ShapeError` would escape instead of returning \"nothing-sent\". The current limits make that unreachable: escaped name, description, reason and the record line stay well under the 4,096-byte content limit. A later field without a client-side check would expose it.\n- The guard filter in `actsFor` packs three conditions into one expression. A named helper would read more easily.\n\nThe Page assets for Counter and Lending change. The planner decides the deployment and checks the hosted pages, as ruling ac586d65 says. No setting changes. This approval authorizes no deployment, publication or live acceptance. D lands last among the DX-T0 heads.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:16022d948393d16538b9c87a3225f2d92c06cbaa","binding":"assigned","head":"4820c13b068bbe7dc8fe68efee60aa1d77ec29ab","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:1819cbde4a4c421c181472da71d2509da984c891\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:00b5bef0936bad3bd01429eb95bd018f11ec717e\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:1819cbde4a4c421c181472da71d2509da984c891","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}